{
  "name": "Occult Association: Gnostic (Tier 2)",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Tier 2 — Gnostic</strong></p><p><strong>“Noise is the enemy.”</strong></p><p>You have learned to reduce interference. Your faction becomes harder to sway, harder to confuse, and harder to redirect with polished lies.</p><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li>Enemy <strong>Soft Power</strong> actions targeting your faction or controlled Hexes suffer <strong>–3 to their OP roll</strong> (minimum 0 penalty floor as adjudicated by the table’s OP logic)</li></ul><p>This does not make you popular. It makes you <em>inconvenient</em>.</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> clarity makes soft control fail, but it also makes diplomacy messier. Expect brittle relationships, exposed tensions, and institutions that resent becoming legible.</p>",
